  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Decent Employment for Youth in Cambodia Phase 3</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Decent Employment for Youth in Cambodia (DEY) programme Phase 3 (DEY III) brings together the combined expertise, skills, resources, comparative advantages and mandates of four participating UN organizations (PUNOs) namely ILO, UNESCO, UNICEF and UNIDO to support Cambodian national partners to achieve the overall objective: more youth in Cambodia are in decent and productive employment by 2028. The programme builds on and aims to maximize the impact of investments made under the Decent Employment for Youth in Cambodia Phase 2 (DEY II) by consolidating and strengthening the most successful and promising interventions, based on national ownership and sustainability at different levels. A continuation from Phase 2, DEY III will be implemented for 4 years from 2024 to 2028. UNESCO will lead the implementation of the Basic Education Equivalency Programme (BEEP).</narrative>
  </description>
